suggestions.suggestionContent:
WHAT: remove(alias) and update(model) dereference a null IdentityProviderModel when the alias/id does not exist and the cache key is already invalidated.
WHY: Throws NullPointerException inside cache handling (registerIDPInvalidation) instead of returning false/no-op, breaking admin remove flows for non-existent aliases.
HOW: Guard: if (storedIdp == null) { registerCountInvalidation(); return idpDelegate.remove(alias); } and in update: IdentityProviderModel idpById = getById(...); if (idpById != null) { registerIDPInvalidation(idpById); registerIDPLoginInvalidationOnUpdate(idpById, model); }

